    {
      "text": "whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her, Matt. 5:28 (3 Ne. 12:28; D&C 42:23; 63:16). Among them that are born of women there hath not risen a greater than John, Matt. 11:11 (Luke 7:28). O woman, great is thy faith, Matt. 15:28. many women were there beholding afar off, Matt. 27:55. Lord is with thee: blessed art thou among women, Luke 1:28 (1:42). woman … brought an alabaster box of ointment, Luke 7:37. Jesus saith … Woman, what have I to do with thee, John 2:4. askest drink of me, which am a woman of Samaria, John 4:9. brought unto him a woman taken in adultery, John 8:3. woman when she is in travail hath sorrow, John 16:21. Woman, behold thy son, John 19:26. Dorcas: this woman was full of good works, Acts 9:36. believed … and of the chief women not a few, Acts 17:4. women did change the natural use, Rom. 1:26. men, leaving the natural use of the woman, Rom. 1:27. It is good for a man not to touch a woman, 1 Cor. 7:1. head of the woman is the man, 1 Cor. 11:3. woman is the glory of the man, 1 Cor. 11:7. neither is the man without the woman, neither the woman without the man, 1 Cor. 11:11. if a woman have long hair, it is a glory, 1 Cor. 11:15. Let your women keep silence in the churches, 1 Cor. 14:34. his Son, made of a woman, Gal. 4:4. women adorn themselves in modest apparel, 1 Tim. 2:9. Let the woman learn in silence, 1 Tim. 2:11. younger women marry, bear children, 1 Tim. 5:14. lead captive silly women laden with sins, 2 Tim. 3:6. aged women likewise, that they be in behaviour, Titus 2:3. teach the young women to be sober, Titus 2:4. Women received their dead raised to life, Heb. 11:35. holy women also, who trusted in God, 1 Pet. 3:5. woman clothed with the sun, Rev. 12:1. not defiled with women; for they are virgins, Rev. 14:4. saw a woman sit upon a scarlet coloured beast, Rev. 17:3.",
